    "body": "Maintainer's decision (question dialog, 2026-11-12) on the case the review of PR #1265 found still open - a turning operation on a MILL-TURN posted through a milling post: **\"Refuse it\"**. Rule: a section that turns the work (a turning op or an on-centre drill, as `lathe_voice::voice_of` reads it) is posted only through a turning post; through a milling post it is refused by name, on a mill-turn as on a lathe. Milling and C-axis sections through a milling post on a mill-turn still post. The shipped Mill-turn machine's default post stays as it is. The existing pin `lathe_workholding_mill_post` (\"posts at the chuck limit\") becomes a refusal test - stricter, not looser.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
